explanation:
`NavigationLink(value: expense)` only records which expense was tapped. `.navigationDestination(for: Expense.self)` tells the enclosing `NavigationStack` what to show for any `Expense` value, so the two work as a pair; without the destination, taps do nothing. `.sheet(isPresented: $isAdding)` presents the form whenever `isAdding` becomes `true`, and sets it back to `false` when the sheet is dismissed.

```swift
NavigationLink(value: expense) { … }
.navigationDestination(for: Expense.self) { … }
.sheet(isPresented: $isAdding) { … }
```
